00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:55.190
Where's the La Fonda Hotel?

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.610
Hotel? Allá está.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:04:59.310
Over where?

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:00.750
Yes, Doc.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:03.400
Thanks.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:31.870
Only 10 cents, no more.

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:35.230
Come, come, to the most beautiful of the walks.

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:36.730
The best of the whole party.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:38.670
Only 10 cents, no more.

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:41.730
We've been here before, but she hasn't.

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:42.920
She hasn't?

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:46.940
Oh, boy, you don't know what you're missing.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:50.820
A walk in the living room, and your eyes will be filled with stars.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.470
You'll see, you'll feel the glory.

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:56.340
Now, before it's too late.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:58.630
Come on, girl, pick your horse.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:05:59.870
Oh, well, to get married...

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:06.910
Talk English? Where's the La Fonda Hotel?

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:11.040
What's the matter? Doesn't anybody know?

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.260
It's over there by the stores.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:14.890
See? Way over there.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.470
Not over there. What's the name of the street?

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:24.540
What's the matter with you? Who you looking at?

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:29.530
You I'm talking to. Who you looking at?

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:34.080
I'll show you the hotel.

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:46.770
Look where you're going.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:50.580
Okay, sitting bull, pick up your feet.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:51.480
Get going. Come on.

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:01.200
There is the hotel.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:03.100
Thanks.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:09.840
Please, take this.

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:13.760
Put it in your pocket. Don't lose it.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:18.160
Her name is Ishton.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.240
My grandmother gave it to me when I come to the city,

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:22.980
so I'm not going to run over.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:25.900
No, I'm not buying any souvenirs.

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:28.210
No, no, you don't buy it. You keep it.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:29.980
Protect me.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:32.540
From what?

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.340
Not at all, ma'am. Positively nothing.

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:03.520
I'm very sure.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.960
Thank you, ma'am. If anything turns up, I have your name.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:08.780
Go and bath for what, please?

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:11.300
Nothing available, sir. Absolutely nothing available.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:13.800
No mail, Mrs. Yosses.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.540
You might try the old Capitan down the street, sir,

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:17.680
but I know they have nothing either.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.000
They're simply nothing available.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:22.220
My name is Blaine. I reserved rooms for four with bath.

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:24.320
Oh, yes, Mr. Blaine. I received your wire.

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:28.030
Hey, bud.

00:08:28.890 --> 00:08:29.430
Yes, sir?

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:30.800
Check that for me, will you?

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:31.840
Be glad to, sir.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:33.300
You wait here.

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:34.400
I'll bring you a check right away.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:34.860
Yeah.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:18.400
Checked out by 3 o'clock, sir. We wouldn't have joined you for an extra day.

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:19.180
Sorry?

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:22.360
Not a thing, sir. We don't have a thing.

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:24.480
Yeah, I know. Will you put that in Mr. Frank Hugo's box?

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:26.420
Oh, yes, sir. Wouldn't you like me to call his room?

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:28.330
No. Just put it in his box.

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:28.950
Yes, sir.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:31.460
Here's a check for your bag, sir.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:34.100
Keep the change.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.140
Oh, thank you, sir.

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:50.490
Yes?

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:52.590
I want to see Frank Hugo.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:56.690
Had you telephoned from downstairs, as is customary, you'd have found that Mr. Hugo is not in.

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:58.280
Is there anything further?

00:09:58.740 --> 00:09:59.820
Nothing I can think of.

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:01.510
And if you'll allow me, I'll close it.

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:05.050
I told you Mr. Hugo's not in.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:22.630
Barber, I'm Mr. Hugo's private secretary.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:24.550
It's too bad, I was gonna ask you for a shave.

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:28.570
You can't wait in Mr. Hugo's room.

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:29.440
Where is he?

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:32.220
If you have no appointment, you'll have to wait downstairs.

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:34.670
I don't like it downstairs. When will he be back?

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:36.450
I said you'll have to wait downstairs.

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:40.430
Now look, if you don't leave this room at once, I'll have to call the manager.

00:10:40.630 --> 00:10:41.430
I wouldn't do that.

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:43.160
Then get out.

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:50.510
Excuse it, please.

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:19.920
Oh, hello. Is Frank in?

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:21.460
No.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:41.080
Did you do that?

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:43.170
He'll be all right.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:45.460
Well, I wasn't worried.

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:48.260
A lot of people would be very grateful to you.

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:50.610
Jonathan can be awfully stuffy.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:52.830
Yeah, I noticed.

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:56.250
Do you mind my asking what you're doing here?

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:57.380
We can kill Frank Hugo.

00:11:58.580 --> 00:11:59.740
He ought to be here in a few minutes.

00:12:00.604 --> 00:12:01.564
I'm having dinner with him.

00:12:02.556 --> 00:12:03.736
Do you expect to join us?

00:12:04.092 --> 00:12:05.812
Look, why don't you just sit down and stop pumping?

00:12:06.204 --> 00:12:06.704
Huh?

00:12:08.092 --> 00:12:10.092
I was just curious.

00:12:19.196 --> 00:12:21.196
You don't intend shooting me, do you?

00:12:26.044 --> 00:12:27.704
Did you really expect to find a gun?

00:12:30.924 --> 00:12:32.384
Heavens, you really did.

00:12:33.452 --> 00:12:35.212
You must lead a fascinating life.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.100
You're not through with me, are you?

00:12:38.572 --> 00:12:40.572
Aren't you going to frisk me?

00:12:41.996 --> 00:12:42.376
Now.

00:12:45.036 --> 00:12:45.656
May I have a light?

00:12:46.284 --> 00:12:46.604
Sure.

00:12:47.692 --> 00:12:48.772
There's one right there on the table.

00:12:53.932 --> 00:12:54.772
Shall I answer that?

00:12:54.772 --> 00:12:55.592
No, I'll get it.

00:13:00.412 --> 00:13:00.912
Hello?

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:02.920
No.

00:13:06.012 --> 00:13:07.312
No, Jonathan's not here.

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:09.660
Yeah.

00:13:10.172 --> 00:13:11.332
This is Mr. Hugo's room.

00:13:13.628 --> 00:13:14.588
Oh, hello, Mr. Hugo.

00:13:17.308 --> 00:13:18.428
No, there's nobody here.

00:13:19.644 --> 00:13:20.844
This is the bellboy speaking.

00:13:22.908 --> 00:13:24.408
I just brought up some ice.

00:13:26.492 --> 00:13:26.952
Yes, sir.

00:13:28.476 --> 00:13:29.476
Yes, sir.

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:33.490
Yeah, I see. Yes, I will.

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:34.860
That was Frank?

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.040
Frank himself.

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:39.380
Police. Call the police.

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:41.860
I don't think this gentleman would approve of that.

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:43.530
Your boss just telephoned.

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:46.300
He said he wouldn't be back until tomorrow.

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:49.280
Well, that's being stood up rather thoroughly.

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:50.490
You're not leaving?

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:51.780
Yeah.

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:53.300
But we could have dinner in the room.

00:13:53.540 --> 00:13:54.620
Frank's already ordered it.

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:55.970
No, thanks.

00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:56.770
I'm sorry.

00:13:56.930 --> 00:13:58.170
I'll be seeing Frank early.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:13:59.360
Who shall I say called?

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:03.820
Just tell him Shorty's pal called, and we'll call again.

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:14.050
Well, there, Mr. Gagin.

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:19.880
How about some lunch? The grill's open.

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:21.150
Who are you?

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:26.250
My name's Ritz. R-E-T-Z. Ritz.

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:27.290
I don't know you.

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:29.790
Well, come along inside. We'll have a cup of coffee.

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:30.860
You get acquainted, Gig.

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:33.450
Got my name, huh?

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:35.120
Oh, I got a lot of things.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:36.780
For instance?

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:39.390
Well, you come in on the 4 o'clock bus,

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:42.420
sat up all the way from Washington, D.C.

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:44.960
That was a cute little chick you put on.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.620
with your note for Frank Hugo to find his room number.

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:49.870
You went up there and waited till he phoned.

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:51.190
He wasn't coming back till tomorrow.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.380
Also, you haven't had any lunch.

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:54.320
Neither have I.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:55.500
How about a bite?

00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:14.860
A cup of coffee and some Danish paste.

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:15.740
Yes, sir.

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:16.940
What are you having, Gagan?

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:18.490
Not a thing.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:19.840
That'll be all, Ed.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:24.560
I guess you know you're not going to find a room in this town.

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:27.860
If Yester's got it filled up to her ears.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.040
Starts tomorrow night.

00:15:31.724 --> 00:15:32.644
Lots of excitement.

00:15:35.276 --> 00:15:35.676
throats.

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:37.000
Dancing in the streets.

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.400
The Indians put on a special show.

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:44.760
You're a cop.

00:15:45.804 --> 00:15:46.804
That's about right.

00:15:47.404 --> 00:15:47.844
Washington.

00:15:49.484 --> 00:15:50.124
Government Cup.

00:15:52.012 --> 00:15:52.672
My mind.

00:15:54.156 --> 00:15:55.656
How come you're tailing me, Uncle Sam?

00:15:57.516 --> 00:15:58.396
Well, thank you, man.

00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:03.920
Excuse me.

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:06.300
Well, I'm not tailing you.

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:09.450
I got in yesterday ahead of you.

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:10.570
Come for the fiesta.

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:12.650
Well, I didn't know about the fiesta.

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:15.360
You and the fiesta are both gravy.

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:18.220
Who's going to ask the questions, me or you?

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:19.540
Go ahead.

00:16:20.740 --> 00:16:22.100
I'm not used to pumping cops.

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:23.270
Well, I don't mind.

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:25.960
How come you know me?

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:29.840
Saw you in Washington at Shorty Thompson's inquest.

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:32.640
Some inquest, that was, huh?

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:35.580
You testified you had no idea who killed your pal.

00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:39.500
Yeah, the cops and I were equally baffled.

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:43.600
I spotted you at the desk here, checked on your rival.

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:46.320
That's the whole mystery, on my end.

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:48.180
Except what you're doing here.

00:16:48.710 --> 00:16:49.990
Well, I'm telling Mr. Hingo.

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:51.330
I thought you knew that.

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:52.960
I don't know anything.

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:55.360
I've been watching him for six months.

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:58.550
You don't watch him very close, do you?

00:16:58.550 --> 00:16:59.970
I mean, you think he kills you.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:03.540
I'll leave the thinking to you, Uncle Sam.

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:06.910
All right, this is what I think.

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:12.260
You're here to square things for Shorty by knocking off Hugo, right?

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:14.240
Go on.

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:17.640
Also, you are as dumb as they come.

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:18.500
I am, huh?

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:22.000
Mr. Hugo's a big man in this part of the world.

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:24.470
He's got lots of friends in this state.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:26.880
He's too tough for you.

00:17:27.180 --> 00:17:27.460
Maybe.

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:29.720
Why don't you smart up?

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:32.390
Leave him to us. We'll get him.

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:35.240
Anything else on your mind?

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:37.160
Oh, don't rush off.

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:42.020
You know, I wouldn't like it a minute if Mr. Hugo got you.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.420
Well, you're not a bad fella.

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:47.400
You like the rest of the boys all cussed up

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:49.540
because you've fought a war for three years

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:51.820
and got nothing out of it but a dangle of ribbons.

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:55.100
Why don't you let your Uncle Samuel take care of him?

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:56.790
How long you been after him?

00:17:57.320 --> 00:17:57.980
A long time.

00:17:58.660 --> 00:17:59.980
Too long to let any...

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:04.720
Yeah. Would be a shame, wouldn't it?

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:07.770
Thanks for the advice, Uncle.

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:10.000
Maybe I sized you up all wrong.

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:12.500
Maybe you're after something else.

00:18:13.710 --> 00:18:15.050
And maybe you're working for Hugo.

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:18.490
I told you I worked for the government.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.000
Doesn't the government work for Hugo?

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:23.500
It did all during the war.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:48.080
If it isn't Jonathan's friend, we send you his love.

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:50.620
Mr. Locke, Mr...

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:51.640
Gagin.

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:53.060
Mr. Gagin.

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:55.710
How do you do? Care to have a drink with us?

00:18:57.270 --> 00:18:58.350
If I was thirsty...

00:18:58.920 --> 00:18:59.980
Maybe he could use a little...

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:02.050
He looks lonely.

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:03.750
I'm a friend of Frank Hugo.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:05.800
I told Mr. Locke about your message.

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:08.220
He's going to talk on the phone with Frank in an hour.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:10.800
We thought you might care to expand it?

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:12.440
No, I don't.

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:16.210
Anything you have to say to Hugo, you can say to me, Mr. Gagan.

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:17.510
Please join us.

00:19:17.770 --> 00:19:19.790
You can hold your drink in your hand if you're not thirsty.

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:21.080
No, thanks.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:26.300
If your business is important, I could tell it to Frank and expedite matters, perhaps.

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:28.870
No, I don't think so.

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:32.840
I'm afraid Mr. Gagin can't be seduced.

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:41.740
See you again, Gagin. Find anything?

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:44.900
No, senor. I've been to all the hotels. They don't have nothing.

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:47.480
No room single, double, nothing empty in San Pablo tonight.

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:48.400
Okay, here.

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:50.440
Oh, gracias, muchas gracias, senor.

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:53.180
Maybe you try tres violetas. You find something there.

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:54.730
What's that, a hotel?

00:19:55.030 --> 00:19:55.970
No, saloon.

00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:58.910
Or maybe some Indian or Mexican have room in his house.

00:19:59.710 --> 00:19:59.970
Pretty cool.

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:03.010
But give them a few bucks, maybe they move.

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:06.380
What is this, whatchamacallit, what's that?

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:08.580
The Tres Violetas. I take you.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:18.520
Here is the Tres Violetas, senor.

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:20.110
Thanks.

00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:22.340
Oh, gracias. Muchas gracias, senor.

00:20:25.810 --> 00:20:26.210
Oh.

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:33.720
You? What are you doing here?

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:35.460
I was waiting.

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:38.140
I'm glad to see you again.

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:39.920
You don't say.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:45.780
I thought I would never see you anymore.

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:48.100
Look, do you know where I can get a room?

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:50.390
A room? Why?

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:51.580
To sleep in.

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:54.820
Mama Mia has a room.

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:55.800
Do you know her?

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:56.940
Yes.

00:20:57.140 --> 00:20:57.660
Where does she live?

00:20:58.690 --> 00:20:59.770
I don't know. I'm lost.

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:01.460
I thought you knew this town.

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:04.630
I know where the La Fonda Hotel was because I passed it before.

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:06.910
I never been to San Pablo before.

00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:09.470
I live in San Mello, 75 miles, very far away.

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:10.210
Okay, okay.

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:13.160
What do you want?

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:16.050
My two friends wonder where they left me.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:16.890
Where'd they go?

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:19.400
Inside, looking for muchachos.

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:19.980
For what?

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:21.410
Boys.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:25.080
Oh, do they know where Mama Mia lives?

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:26.800
I don't know what they know.

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:27.720
Thanks.

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:31.950
Maybe I'll go with you.

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:34.160
No, not tonight, sitting boy.

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:35.780
You will need me, senor.

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:39.440
Look, there's something going on inside your head.

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:40.320
What's going on in there, huh?

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:41.440
Nothing, senor, nothing.

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:42.540
Only I...

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:45.100
I don't know what to do tonight.

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:47.360
Why don't you get yourself a muchacho,

00:21:48.060 --> 00:21:48.640
like your girlfriend?

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:51.390
I don't know how.

00:21:53.300 --> 00:21:53.840
Telling me.

00:22:39.980 --> 00:22:40.760
Excuse me.

00:22:41.320 --> 00:22:42.820
Oh, es el amigo de Pila.

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:45.840
Yeah, I was talking to your friend outside.

00:22:46.280 --> 00:22:46.700
Pila?

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.370
Oh, all night she will be outside.

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:50.770
She's crazy.

00:22:51.650 --> 00:22:52.630
Yeah, I wouldn't be surprised.

00:22:53.620 --> 00:22:55.000
She said something about Mama Mia.

00:22:55.340 --> 00:22:56.120
Do you know where she lives?

00:22:56.580 --> 00:22:57.800
Oh, sí, I know where she lives.

00:22:58.120 --> 00:22:58.800
I take you.

00:22:59.580 --> 00:22:59.980
She don't...

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.200
I don't know nothing about Mama Mia.

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:06.140
Excuse me.

00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:26.680
No, I want a big whiskey. Big one. Big one.

00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:33.570
Sí, señor, sí. Sí, sí.

00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:44.900
Tequila.

00:23:48.560 --> 00:23:51.300
No change, señor. Too big. Too big. No change.

00:23:51.990 --> 00:23:53.190
That's the smallest thing I got.

00:23:53.450 --> 00:23:54.190
No change.

00:23:54.810 --> 00:23:57.830
Qué hombre, se toma mi tequila y me da este billete y no tengo el vuelto.

00:23:57.930 --> 00:23:58.730
Pues qué voy a hacer?

00:23:59.170 --> 00:23:59.670
¿Cuánto es?

00:24:00.060 --> 00:24:02.640
20 pesos. Viene aquí, toma un trago y me da este billete.

00:24:02.780 --> 00:24:04.620
¿Qué cree que es aquí, el Banco de México?

00:24:04.840 --> 00:24:06.200
Si yo tuviera todo ese dinero, yo...

00:24:06.200 --> 00:24:08.510
Oh, espérate, hermano. No te opures.

00:24:09.240 --> 00:24:12.020
Pancho te ayudará. ¿Cuánto cambio tienes?

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:16.640
10 pesos, pero no tengo suficiente para 20.

00:24:17.280 --> 00:24:18.260
¿Quién cree que soy yo?

00:24:18.360 --> 00:24:19.820
Oh, silencio, silencio.

00:24:21.670 --> 00:24:24.100
Señor, my name is Pancho.

00:24:25.050 --> 00:24:26.090
I would like to help you.

00:24:27.210 --> 00:24:28.310
I will be your friend.

00:24:29.130 --> 00:24:29.970
I'll tell you what I...

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:30.520
What are you going to do?

00:24:36.520 --> 00:24:38.060
It's 20 pesos.

00:24:38.580 --> 00:24:39.620
It's your 20.

00:24:40.600 --> 00:24:45.430
He can change only 10.

00:24:46.700 --> 00:24:52.110
So, we drink 10 and everybody is happy.

00:24:53.180 --> 00:24:54.800
You want to make everybody happy, see?

00:24:56.180 --> 00:24:58.000
Sure, let's make everybody happy.

00:25:00.090 --> 00:25:02.170
Thank you very much.

00:25:07.070 --> 00:25:09.590
Don't mind whiskey, I don't want to burn a hole in my neck.

00:25:12.180 --> 00:25:14.620
Amigo, you are the blood of my heart.

00:25:15.160 --> 00:25:17.110
You are true friend to you.

00:25:17.810 --> 00:25:18.210
Salud!

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:33.540
La musica, la musica. Manito. Fill up my friend's glass.

00:25:33.860 --> 00:25:37.600
Full, big. The big drinks is most best.

00:25:39.440 --> 00:25:40.830
Hey, listen.

00:25:42.770 --> 00:25:45.370
You know why that man sing miamido?

00:25:46.110 --> 00:25:49.650
He sings because tomorrow we burn sa sobra.

00:25:50.130 --> 00:25:52.130
He's the god of bad luck.

00:25:52.350 --> 00:25:54.990
He's got face more worse than me.

00:25:56.290 --> 00:25:58.490
Tomorrow we burn sa sobra.

00:25:58.690 --> 00:25:59.960
And we have...

00:26:00.120 --> 00:26:03.240
No more bad luck.

00:26:08.420 --> 00:26:09.980
Big drink for everybody.

00:26:13.960 --> 00:26:18.300
What did you say? So quick, we drink up all the change.

00:26:18.560 --> 00:26:19.680
There's a lot more where it came from.

00:26:22.370 --> 00:26:27.270
When I see you, I say, this is kind of fellow more proud than you, Pancho.

00:26:27.710 --> 00:26:29.370
Pancho, a very proud man.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:33.770
Hey, chato, give me a drink. Big drink for everybody.

00:26:33.970 --> 00:26:34.950
Pancho is buying.

00:26:37.470 --> 00:26:39.850
You lend me $10. I'll pay you tomorrow.

00:26:42.670 --> 00:26:44.690
Amigo, my beautiful amiga.

00:26:45.130 --> 00:26:47.190
You got the kind of face I like.

00:26:48.280 --> 00:26:49.820
You come in here for something.

00:26:50.660 --> 00:26:53.280
You tell Panchito what you look for, he get it for you.

00:26:53.810 --> 00:26:55.450
Yeah, you tell Panchito.

00:26:55.710 --> 00:26:57.170
I'm looking for a place to sleep in.

00:26:58.600 --> 00:26:59.980
What? You got no place?

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:00.740
No.

00:27:01.400 --> 00:27:04.460
Oye, muchachos, el amigo de Pancho no tiene donde dormir.

00:27:04.780 --> 00:27:05.120
Oh!

00:27:06.500 --> 00:27:10.300
That's the kind of man I like, the man with no place.

00:27:11.320 --> 00:27:14.980
I will give you the most fine place to sleep in all of Mexico.

00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:15.820
San Pablo.

00:27:17.140 --> 00:27:18.020
And your man.

00:27:18.240 --> 00:27:19.000
Fill him up.

00:27:19.100 --> 00:27:19.540
All right.

00:27:19.540 --> 00:27:19.840
Thank you.

00:27:19.840 --> 00:27:20.740
Thank you.

00:27:22.960 --> 00:27:23.400
Salud.

00:27:23.400 --> 00:27:23.720
Salud.

00:27:24.480 --> 00:27:24.920
Salud.

00:27:25.140 --> 00:27:25.580
Salud.

