00:27:34.320 --> 00:27:38.110
Hey, what's the matter? You don't feel good?

00:27:38.540 --> 00:27:41.940
You drink whole bottle and don't feel good. That's bad.

00:27:42.220 --> 00:27:44.610
Amigo, I feel fine.

00:27:44.850 --> 00:27:46.250
No, something is wrong.

00:27:46.920 --> 00:27:48.720
I sing and something says,

00:27:48.920 --> 00:27:51.520
Poncho, shut up. That's you.

00:27:51.720 --> 00:27:52.920
I didn't tell you to shut up.

00:27:53.040 --> 00:27:55.080
Your heart tells me. What's the matter?

00:27:55.180 --> 00:27:56.680
You're not Poncho's friend.

00:27:57.150 --> 00:27:58.190
I'm nobody's friend.

00:27:58.670 --> 00:27:58.990
Hey.

00:28:00.670 --> 00:28:01.190
What's the matter?

00:28:02.020 --> 00:28:03.120
Somebody follow us.

00:28:04.250 --> 00:28:05.150
I don't hear nobody.

00:28:06.380 --> 00:28:07.800
Somebody walk soft.

00:28:12.070 --> 00:28:13.170
Oh, it's a girl.

00:28:14.790 --> 00:28:16.900
Oh, she no good, too skinny.

00:28:17.860 --> 00:28:19.900
I told you once before, tonight, no dice.

00:28:20.670 --> 00:28:21.930
Oh, she your girl, eh?

00:28:22.090 --> 00:28:22.770
I don't know her.

00:28:23.400 --> 00:28:25.460
That's all right, you could tell, Poncho.

00:28:26.000 --> 00:28:27.840
I don't know her, I tell you, and I don't want to know her.

00:28:28.450 --> 00:28:29.970
Now go on home and play with your buffers.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:34.480
Hey, that's right. She's too skinny. No good.

00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:38.520
Ah, them kids. The fiesta bring them like honey.

00:28:38.900 --> 00:28:43.260
They come for sing, for dance, for get fella, have a good time,

00:28:43.440 --> 00:28:46.560
then go home and pull the plow for a year.

00:28:47.740 --> 00:28:51.360
That one pretty skinny. You get much better more later on.

00:28:51.700 --> 00:28:55.240
Hey! Skin... Oh, she gone.

00:28:56.080 --> 00:28:58.140
My goodness. Where's she gone?

00:29:00.160 --> 00:29:01.900
Y yo ya me ooooy

00:29:02.340 --> 00:29:03.400
HA HA HA

00:29:03.400 --> 00:29:05.110
AL PUERTA

00:29:08.160 --> 00:29:09.000
LA BOI

00:29:20.550 --> 00:29:23.370
Hey, where we goin?

00:29:24.600 --> 00:29:25.260
I'll show ya

00:29:35.790 --> 00:29:36.390
Where's the house?

00:29:37.270 --> 00:29:38.410
The house, senor.

00:29:41.940 --> 00:29:42.840
You're drunk.

00:29:43.190 --> 00:29:44.090
It's possible.

00:29:46.050 --> 00:29:48.710
But never too drunk for know my own house.

00:29:49.870 --> 00:29:50.390
Have a look.

00:29:51.020 --> 00:29:52.460
The Palace of Poncho.

00:29:53.200 --> 00:29:54.400
That's a fine ceiling.

00:29:55.200 --> 00:29:56.380
That's good walls.

00:29:57.770 --> 00:29:58.910
Beautiful landlord.

00:30:01.600 --> 00:30:05.650
Momentito. Especial for you.

00:30:06.420 --> 00:30:07.700
Here. Give me the bottle.

00:30:08.660 --> 00:30:09.940
How you like my house, amigo?

00:30:10.520 --> 00:30:13.500
I've been in worse houses. Who owns that outfit?

00:30:14.490 --> 00:30:16.380
Tio Vivo. She's mine.

00:30:17.260 --> 00:30:20.850
I own everything. 12 beautiful horses,

00:30:21.660 --> 00:30:24.480
three beautiful chariots, whole beautiful orchestra.

00:30:24.860 --> 00:30:29.080
All panchas. Hey, you drink pretty good for a gringo.

00:30:30.060 --> 00:30:34.780
Yeah, some people's happy when they got money.

00:30:35.420 --> 00:30:38.680
Me, I'm only happy when I got nothing.

00:30:40.260 --> 00:30:41.900
Nothing? And a friend.

00:30:43.140 --> 00:30:45.680
So long as Poncho got somebody he can tell,

00:30:46.620 --> 00:30:50.400
amigo, I love you, that's enough.

00:30:52.180 --> 00:30:54.460
Hey, they can keep everything else.

00:30:55.210 --> 00:30:59.430
Keep the whole world. Give Poncho...

00:31:00.600 --> 00:31:02.320
Ale, Pancho.

00:31:05.440 --> 00:31:08.540
Buenas noches, mi amigo.

00:31:44.650 --> 00:31:59.300
you want huh you want a ride yes wait a minute i'll wake up fatso hey aren't you

00:32:00.090 --> 00:32:00.710
You got a customer?

00:32:01.410 --> 00:32:02.230
Oh, close it.

00:32:02.390 --> 00:32:03.230
No more customers.

00:32:03.530 --> 00:32:04.590
Come on, come on, get up.

00:32:05.410 --> 00:32:06.790
I tell you, she's too skinny.

00:32:07.470 --> 00:32:08.950
Lots more better manana.

00:32:09.340 --> 00:32:10.940
Come on, Pancho, she wants a ride.

00:32:11.060 --> 00:32:11.580
Turn it, will you?

00:32:11.680 --> 00:32:12.600
No, no, no ride.

00:32:12.780 --> 00:32:14.620
It's late, Tio Vivo, close it.

00:32:15.170 --> 00:32:16.570
Music wake the people.

00:32:16.730 --> 00:32:18.530
Okay, no music, but turn it, huh?

00:32:19.100 --> 00:32:20.980
No, I don't give no free ride.

00:32:21.180 --> 00:32:21.880
It's rule.

00:32:22.140 --> 00:32:22.740
Break the rule.

00:32:23.870 --> 00:32:26.350
10 centavos, 10 centavos, one ride.

00:32:26.650 --> 00:32:27.350
Okay, yeah.

00:32:28.690 --> 00:32:29.770
Muchas gracias, señor.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:37.120
Did you ever ride on one of them before?

00:32:37.820 --> 00:32:38.140
No.

00:32:39.440 --> 00:32:40.880
Well, go on. Get going. Go on.

00:32:42.030 --> 00:32:42.610
Which one?

00:32:53.220 --> 00:32:53.660
The pink one.

00:33:17.280 --> 00:33:21.680
Okay, sitting ball, why don't you give us a war hoop, you know.

00:33:42.030 --> 00:33:42.590
That's all.

00:33:43.240 --> 00:33:45.720
Dear Saint-Tavis, 10 cents. One ride.

00:33:53.430 --> 00:33:55.600
Ishtel, the good goddess.

00:33:56.590 --> 00:33:57.350
What's she good for?

00:33:57.830 --> 00:33:59.910
Keep away death. Very fine.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:09.650
Charm I got a better charm soldier gun why best charm in the world keeps away the boogeyman

00:34:39.020 --> 00:34:39.700
Someone is here.

00:34:41.800 --> 00:34:42.180
What?

00:34:42.650 --> 00:34:43.490
Someone is here.

00:34:47.870 --> 00:34:48.330
Who's here?

00:34:48.840 --> 00:34:49.960
Someone is hiding out there.

00:35:01.790 --> 00:35:02.230
Gagan?

00:35:02.570 --> 00:35:02.930
Yeah.

00:35:03.890 --> 00:35:08.660
Sorry to wake you up, but I got to thinking maybe we ought to have a little talk.

00:35:10.140 --> 00:35:11.560
We had a talk, Uncle Sam.

00:35:12.000 --> 00:35:13.780
Sure, but another one.

00:35:14.680 --> 00:35:16.460
I got a couple of new ideas.

00:35:21.780 --> 00:35:22.820
Go on, beat it. Scramble.

00:35:24.170 --> 00:35:25.530
Go on over there, way over there.

00:35:37.580 --> 00:35:41.120
I told you I didn't want you removing Mr. Hugo from the scene.

00:35:42.650 --> 00:35:46.410
But I ain't about that anymore. Not the way you're handling it.

00:35:47.160 --> 00:35:51.280
Walking in there and telling him Shorty's pal is looking for it.

00:35:51.890 --> 00:35:52.950
Playing it tough, huh?

00:35:54.270 --> 00:35:56.770
They've got a couple of bad boys out looking for you.

00:35:57.290 --> 00:35:58.050
This interest you?

00:35:58.480 --> 00:35:59.620
Yeah, kinda.

00:36:00.480 --> 00:36:05.100
Those mugs that Mr. Locke put on you will be around at the Three Violettos when it opens.

00:36:05.760 --> 00:36:07.580
They'll find out the same lead I did.

00:36:09.460 --> 00:36:10.440
What time does it open?

00:36:11.180 --> 00:36:14.640
Around nine. I got an extra bed in my room.

00:36:15.490 --> 00:36:16.950
You'll be a little more comfortable there.

00:36:19.380 --> 00:36:22.100
No, I'll stay here.

00:36:24.750 --> 00:36:26.610
Kind of figured I was wasting my time.

00:36:28.170 --> 00:36:28.670
Hey, Rich.

00:36:29.120 --> 00:36:29.340
Yeah?

00:36:31.530 --> 00:36:33.190
Thanks. Don't mention it.

00:37:04.730 --> 00:37:07.910
But it's a rubia, but it's a rubia, but it's a rubia,

00:37:08.010 --> 00:37:09.350
me gustammas.

00:37:10.140 --> 00:37:15.120
Hey, fine, beautiful morning, mi amigo.

00:37:15.390 --> 00:37:15.970
How you feel?

00:37:16.560 --> 00:37:16.960
Fine.

00:37:17.840 --> 00:37:19.840
How you sleep in Pancho's Palas, eh?

00:37:19.920 --> 00:37:20.620
Like a baby, eh?

00:37:20.800 --> 00:37:21.500
Yeah, like a baby.

00:37:21.600 --> 00:37:22.520
Where'd you get this razor?

00:37:22.870 --> 00:37:24.110
It's a very fine razor.

00:37:24.500 --> 00:37:26.200
I shaved with it myself once.

00:37:27.040 --> 00:37:28.020
What time is it?

00:37:30.600 --> 00:37:31.620
About 10 minutes past 7.

00:37:31.760 --> 00:37:32.100
Oh.

00:37:33.400 --> 00:37:35.240
I have a fine dream last night.

00:37:35.860 --> 00:37:38.040
I dream all my horses is alive.

00:37:38.520 --> 00:37:41.620
And we all riding on desert for hunting lions.

00:37:42.780 --> 00:37:44.790
And I am young again.

00:37:47.520 --> 00:37:49.560
Ay, la flaquita.

00:37:57.130 --> 00:37:57.750
Service, eh?

00:37:58.500 --> 00:37:59.900
Where you get that new bucket?

00:38:02.320 --> 00:38:03.820
It's a very fine bucket.

00:38:04.520 --> 00:38:07.520
It's a sign of good luck when you find a new bucket.

00:38:07.860 --> 00:38:08.000
Yeah?

00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:14.510
Got a looking glass. Small one.

00:38:15.230 --> 00:38:16.890
I don't need it. I'm all through.

00:38:25.040 --> 00:38:26.320
Why do you have to look like that?

00:38:27.200 --> 00:38:27.700
Like what?

00:38:28.730 --> 00:38:29.970
Like you come out of a side shop.

00:38:31.400 --> 00:38:32.500
What's a sad show?

00:38:33.210 --> 00:38:34.290
Place where they keep freaks.

00:38:35.320 --> 00:38:36.200
I look like a freak?

00:38:36.640 --> 00:38:37.740
You look like Zip. What is it?

00:38:39.070 --> 00:38:40.090
Why do I look like that?

00:38:40.950 --> 00:38:43.700
I don't know. Maybe it's a dress.

00:38:44.290 --> 00:38:45.650
This is my grandmother's dress.

00:38:46.550 --> 00:38:48.430
She gave it to me when I come to the fiesta.

00:38:50.040 --> 00:38:51.900
I never had a dress so nice as this.

00:38:54.820 --> 00:38:57.100
Might be all right if you took some of them spangles off it.

00:38:58.920 --> 00:38:59.660
Take them off.

00:39:01.790 --> 00:39:03.210
You might also comb your hair.

00:39:04.350 --> 00:39:07.260
Hair is not right.

00:39:07.620 --> 00:39:09.060
All right for mice to sleep in.

00:39:10.490 --> 00:39:11.130
Give me my coat.

00:39:26.700 --> 00:39:29.960
Here, go get yourself a permanent wave or something.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:31.930
Maybe a manicure, huh?

00:39:32.940 --> 00:39:34.560
No. I can't take the money.

00:39:34.680 --> 00:39:36.890
Why not? It's too much.

00:39:38.370 --> 00:39:41.800
Count. That's something, huh? Go on, take it. Make yourself look human.

00:39:42.850 --> 00:39:45.240
You'll like me if I look human?

00:39:45.940 --> 00:39:49.380
Look, sitting bull, I'm not buying any trouble this trip.

00:39:50.070 --> 00:39:53.590
I got other things on my mind. Go on now, beat it.

00:40:01.600 --> 00:40:05.750
Ten dollar? Mi amigo, you crazy for waste time on a stick.

00:40:06.140 --> 00:40:08.720
Fella like you can get princess, fat one.

00:40:09.270 --> 00:40:13.770
Yeah, I've had princesses, all kinds. I got one now, back east.

00:40:14.630 --> 00:40:16.790
That's crazy. Why you don't bring her to the fiesta?

00:40:18.420 --> 00:40:21.340
She's busy with another guy.

00:40:22.420 --> 00:40:24.860
I don't think I like him, that other guy.

00:40:25.180 --> 00:40:29.820
Ah, don't say that. He's okay. He's got what it takes.

00:40:30.510 --> 00:40:31.310
Dope.

00:41:28.090 --> 00:41:28.550
You go in.

00:41:30.640 --> 00:41:31.800
I said, is Mr. Hugo in?

00:41:31.900 --> 00:41:32.300
Who is it?

00:41:32.420 --> 00:41:34.520
The man who was here yesterday, sir.

00:41:34.660 --> 00:41:35.940
No, shorty's pal. Let him in.

00:41:36.460 --> 00:41:37.680
Mr. Hugo will see you.

00:41:41.780 --> 00:41:43.380
You want me to come back for the shampoo, senor?

00:41:43.400 --> 00:41:44.060
I'll call you later.

00:41:44.580 --> 00:41:45.280
Gracias, senor.

00:41:46.390 --> 00:41:47.490
Mr. Locke in his room?

00:41:47.670 --> 00:41:49.630
No, Mr. Hugo. He left ten minutes ago.

00:41:49.790 --> 00:41:50.450
Wait downstairs.

00:41:50.630 --> 00:41:50.890
Yes, sir.

00:41:51.330 --> 00:41:52.210
You want me in, boss?

00:41:52.310 --> 00:41:52.750
No, out.

00:41:56.780 --> 00:41:58.100
Now, Mr. Gagin, what can I do for you?

00:42:04.990 --> 00:42:08.320
Yes, Mr. Hugo. No, I can't talk to him now.

00:42:08.710 --> 00:42:09.990
No more calls for it, you know.

00:42:10.130 --> 00:42:14.150
What do you like to look around?

00:42:15.270 --> 00:42:16.110
I don't mind company.

00:42:17.180 --> 00:42:22.290
Sit down. I'm glad to see you, Mr. Gagan.

00:42:23.280 --> 00:42:24.540
How's our friend, Mr. Retz?

00:42:25.560 --> 00:42:26.120
He's okay.

00:42:26.660 --> 00:42:27.880
I hear you've been talking to him.

00:42:28.940 --> 00:42:29.940
How would I have to talk to him?

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:39.900
I don't know I'm right in arms you're both shooting at the same target aren't you he's no pal of mine good for you cigar

00:42:39.900 --> 00:42:48.750
No, thanks. So you're shorty's pal. That's right shorty was a nice guy

00:42:48.750 --> 00:42:54.510
Yeah, he was say what you in the same outfit together Pacific area

00:42:54.510 --> 00:42:59.600
I got a soft spot for ex-servicemen tried to get in myself. Too bad. They had to turn you down

00:43:03.320 --> 00:43:05.480
I gave Shorty a job when he got out, a good job.

00:43:06.500 --> 00:43:07.140
Yeah, I know.

00:43:07.370 --> 00:43:10.030
A hundred a week just to see that people didn't bother me too much.

00:43:10.380 --> 00:43:12.320
Should have solved all his post-war problems.

00:43:13.000 --> 00:43:15.260
Too bad your pal Shorty turned out to be a crook.

00:43:16.120 --> 00:43:18.360
Got himself all crumbed up, reaching for easy money.

00:43:19.540 --> 00:43:23.960
That's kind of funny talk coming from a guy who's done rather well out of the government.

00:43:25.010 --> 00:43:26.490
Kind of like spitting in my own face.

00:43:26.630 --> 00:43:27.850
That's what you're thinking, isn't it, Gagan?

00:43:28.850 --> 00:43:29.350
I'm thinking.

00:43:31.210 --> 00:43:34.330
Our friend Shorty was the kind of a crook that nobody likes, not even me,

00:43:34.430 --> 00:43:36.530
who I'm rather broad-minded about such things.

00:43:37.910 --> 00:43:39.090
I'll lay it on the line, Gagan.

00:43:39.560 --> 00:43:41.720
Shorty took something from me and tried to sell it back.

00:43:42.070 --> 00:43:44.790
I don't like blackmailers, nor would you if you were in my business.

00:43:44.970 --> 00:43:47.430
They constitute a very bad industrial hazard.

00:43:48.640 --> 00:43:51.020
I wanted what Shorty had. He refused to give it to me.

00:43:51.100 --> 00:43:51.680
There was a fight.

00:43:52.500 --> 00:43:54.680
Your pal Shorty wasn't as tough as he thought he was.

00:43:55.230 --> 00:43:56.090
So you had him killed.

00:43:56.850 --> 00:43:58.510
Let's put it that he lost the argument.

00:43:58.860 --> 00:43:59.980
The three guys with blackjack.

00:44:01.180 --> 00:44:01.760
Were there three?

00:44:02.210 --> 00:44:03.850
And three pretty stupid guys, too.

00:44:04.260 --> 00:44:04.560
Stupid?

00:44:05.040 --> 00:44:05.300
Yeah.

00:44:05.960 --> 00:44:07.180
They didn't get what they were after.

00:44:07.420 --> 00:44:07.840
They didn't?

00:44:08.060 --> 00:44:08.360
No.

00:44:08.810 --> 00:44:09.330
I got it.

00:44:10.970 --> 00:44:13.730
A canceled check for a hundred grand on a Mexican bank,

00:44:13.940 --> 00:44:14.800
signed by you,

00:44:16.220 --> 00:44:19.240
and made out to a guy who was making patriotic speeches

00:44:19.240 --> 00:44:22.360
about the time I was getting a tan in a place called New Guinea.

00:44:23.000 --> 00:44:24.760
You sound like a disillusioned patriot.

00:44:25.720 --> 00:44:27.200
The number of the check is 6431.

00:44:29.620 --> 00:44:29.980
You've got...

00:44:31.680 --> 00:44:32.820
It wouldn't be on you, would it?

00:44:34.330 --> 00:44:35.970
No, of course not. You wouldn't be that dumb.

00:44:37.730 --> 00:44:39.210
All right, Mr. Gagan, how much do you want?

00:44:39.780 --> 00:44:42.520
30 grand. Shorty only wanted 15.

00:44:43.260 --> 00:44:45.300
The extra 15 is an account of Shorty.

00:44:45.620 --> 00:44:47.960
A real friend. Don't kid yourself.

00:44:48.120 --> 00:44:49.660
You're doing it for Shorty, you're doing it for you,

00:44:49.780 --> 00:44:51.200
just like I did what I did for me.

00:44:51.690 --> 00:44:54.350
Look, do I get the 30 grand or do I turn the check over to Mr. Retz?

00:44:54.470 --> 00:44:55.470
So that's the way it's gonna be.

00:44:55.570 --> 00:44:56.510
That's the way it's gonna be.

00:44:57.660 --> 00:44:59.970
Look, Gagan, let's hit it on the nose. You and me...

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:01.240
we eat out of the same dish.

00:45:01.760 --> 00:45:03.520
You used to think if you were a square guy,

00:45:03.700 --> 00:45:04.820
worked hard, played on the level,

00:45:04.920 --> 00:45:05.840
things had come your way.

00:45:05.920 --> 00:45:06.960
You found out you were wrong.

00:45:07.470 --> 00:45:08.530
All you get is pushed around.

00:45:09.250 --> 00:45:11.170
You found that people are interested in only one thing,

00:45:11.290 --> 00:45:11.710
the payoff.

00:45:13.010 --> 00:45:14.230
That's all I'm interested in.

00:45:14.330 --> 00:45:15.110
That's the idea.

00:45:15.880 --> 00:45:17.060
You know, Gagan, I like you.

00:45:17.640 --> 00:45:19.280
There are two kinds of people in this world.

00:45:19.600 --> 00:45:21.040
Ones that fiddle around worrying whether

00:45:21.040 --> 00:45:23.000
are things right or wrong, and guys like us.

00:45:23.140 --> 00:45:25.020
Do I get the 30 grand or do I drop it on you?

00:45:25.040 --> 00:45:26.380
It's going to be a pretty hot 30 grand.

00:45:26.500 --> 00:45:27.180
You sure you want it?

00:45:27.970 --> 00:45:28.530
I'm sure.

00:45:29.130 --> 00:45:29.970
You know, the spot you...

00:45:30.280 --> 00:45:32.000
I'd be a dope to pay blackmail.

00:45:33.020 --> 00:45:34.000
What'll you be if you don't?

00:45:34.180 --> 00:45:36.640
The blackmailer might have a photostatic copy of the check.

00:45:36.800 --> 00:45:37.780
Then you have to pay again.

00:45:38.380 --> 00:45:40.220
Now, he may remember the check number in the bank

00:45:40.220 --> 00:45:41.480
and give that information to Retz.

00:45:42.010 --> 00:45:44.550
I'd be buying practically nothing for my 30 grand but a headache.

00:45:45.680 --> 00:45:48.680
20 years in the jug for stealing from the government is also a headache.

00:45:48.840 --> 00:45:51.860
It's worth thinking about.

00:45:52.980 --> 00:45:55.380
You know, I'm getting kind of tired of having that check haunt me.

00:45:55.500 --> 00:45:57.840
I think I'll take a chance on you being a square blackmailer.

00:45:57.940 --> 00:45:59.400
I'll give you 15 grand. 30.

00:46:01.370 --> 00:46:03.950
I came down here to enjoy the fiesta. I'll charge it up to pleasure.

00:46:04.750 --> 00:46:06.070
You'll want it in cash, naturally.

00:46:06.350 --> 00:46:07.330
Right here in my hand.

00:46:07.530 --> 00:46:09.090
I don't carry that kind of money with me.

00:46:09.210 --> 00:46:11.230
It'll take me a few hours to get it. Where can I reach you?

00:46:11.380 --> 00:46:11.700
Here.

00:46:12.220 --> 00:46:14.020
I'd rather you didn't clutter up my rooms.

00:46:14.890 --> 00:46:17.050
I'll have the money around, say, 7 o'clock. See you then.

00:46:17.820 --> 00:46:19.440
Couldn't we find someplace more public?

00:46:19.640 --> 00:46:20.180
More public?

00:46:22.410 --> 00:46:24.350
It's a sensible precaution.

00:46:25.180 --> 00:46:26.600
You know where the Tip Top Cafe is?

00:46:27.040 --> 00:46:27.700
I'll find it.

00:46:28.160 --> 00:46:29.280
And you'll have that little item.

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:31.380
You'll get the check when I get the dough.

00:46:32.170 --> 00:46:34.400
It's me too. I don't even trust my mother.

00:46:34.930 --> 00:46:36.790
And I guess a blackmailer can't be too careful.

00:46:37.500 --> 00:46:40.080
Must be an exciting way to make a living. I'll have to try it sometime.

00:46:42.610 --> 00:46:48.160
I'll see you at the Tip Top Cafe at 7 o'clock.

00:47:00.440 --> 00:47:01.020
Good morning.

00:47:04.540 --> 00:47:08.140
Waiting for your friend? Known him long?

00:47:09.960 --> 00:47:10.400
Yesterday.

00:47:11.380 --> 00:47:15.110
You like him? Why don't you help him? He's in trouble.

00:47:17.140 --> 00:47:17.620
I know.

00:47:18.700 --> 00:47:20.440
You mean you know the kind of trouble he's in?

00:47:21.680 --> 00:47:22.020
Yes.

00:47:22.520 --> 00:47:24.280
What kind of trouble would you say it is?

00:47:25.780 --> 00:47:27.060
He will die, maybe.

00:47:27.790 --> 00:47:29.440
Yeah? When?

00:47:31.080 --> 00:47:31.480
Soon.

00:47:31.900 --> 00:47:32.540
How soon?

00:47:33.830 --> 00:47:34.490
Before long.

00:47:35.370 --> 00:47:36.190
How do you get that?

00:47:37.730 --> 00:47:38.290
I saw.

00:47:39.160 --> 00:47:39.860
What did you see?

00:47:41.800 --> 00:47:42.740
I saw him dead.

00:47:43.550 --> 00:47:44.810
Beats me how you get that.

00:47:44.970 --> 00:47:45.850
You saw him dead?

00:47:46.810 --> 00:47:48.110
Or you mean you dreamed it?

00:47:49.400 --> 00:47:51.220
No, I saw it.

00:47:52.420 --> 00:47:57.220
Yesterday when he came to the medical room, I saw his face, dead.

00:47:58.320 --> 00:47:59.960
His eyes were closed, the skin...

00:48:00.060 --> 00:48:07.970
was white. He was dead. Not a bad hunch. I don't see things like that, but I got it figured my way.

00:48:08.780 --> 00:48:20.660
Listen, I'm trying to help him. You believe that? If he tells me. Hiya, Rats. Why, hello there.

00:48:21.400 --> 00:48:26.790
I've just been talking to your friend. How'd you like to take a walk? Lots of fiesta doing starting out.

00:48:27.140 --> 00:48:29.810
No, I'm not here for the fiesta either.

00:48:30.350 --> 00:48:34.140
That's what I figured. You didn't come for the show. You come for the money.

00:48:34.750 --> 00:48:37.690
You know, I've been a little slow on the pick-up. I don't know why.

00:48:38.350 --> 00:48:40.790
I just didn't figure you for a shakedown job.

00:48:41.780 --> 00:48:46.500
I'm after Hugo. You've got some evidence that can help me send him up.

00:48:46.760 --> 00:48:50.210
I haven't any idea what it is. You're trying to sell it to him.

00:48:50.760 --> 00:48:53.860
But the chances are 10 to 1. You'll wind up like Shorty.

00:48:55.050 --> 00:48:59.980
I'm asking you for that evidence. Officially. See how?

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:04.440
I'm not talking for myself. I'm talking, like you say, for Uncle Sam.

00:49:04.760 --> 00:49:06.700
You tell Uncle Sam to go take a walk for himself.

00:49:07.880 --> 00:49:11.940
And look, Hopper, don't wave any flags at me. I've seen enough flags.

00:49:13.570 --> 00:49:14.710
I've spoken my piece.

00:49:15.100 --> 00:49:18.590
And I've heard enough pieces, too. They don't register anymore.

00:49:19.620 --> 00:49:21.560
Okay, soldier.

00:49:21.860 --> 00:49:24.160
I'll be seeing you around.

00:49:24.460 --> 00:49:25.400
I'll be around.

00:49:35.910 --> 00:49:42.290
What happened to you?

00:49:43.310 --> 00:49:47.140
Do you like? Do I look human?

00:49:49.880 --> 00:49:50.980
What else should I do?

00:49:51.770 --> 00:49:53.750
You can't do anything else. You've done everything.

00:49:53.950 --> 00:49:56.380
You hungry?

00:49:57.290 --> 00:49:58.230
I ate an apple.

00:49:58.470 --> 00:49:59.510
No, no, no. I mean food.

00:50:01.400 --> 00:50:03.460
Come on, it's a little early, but we'll have some lunch, huh?

00:50:05.200 --> 00:50:06.810
Where? In the restaurant.

00:50:07.490 --> 00:50:10.770
Oh, no, no, I can't. Why not?

00:50:13.090 --> 00:50:14.230
What's the matter? Don't you answer questions?

00:50:15.820 --> 00:50:17.300
Ah, you don't have to be afraid of a restaurant.

00:50:18.460 --> 00:50:19.620
It's not gonna bite you or scalp you.

00:50:20.050 --> 00:50:22.350
All you have to do is walk in and sit down and pretend you're a human being.

00:50:22.910 --> 00:50:24.450
This way, please. Yeah, I want to sit over there.

00:50:34.600 --> 00:50:34.980
Hey.

00:50:52.860 --> 00:50:54.140
See anything you want?

00:50:57.040 --> 00:50:58.620
Look, if you can't read, say so.

00:51:00.420 --> 00:51:04.710
Go ahead and read it. See if there's anything you want to eat.

00:51:09.710 --> 00:51:10.470
I'm not hungry.

00:51:10.710 --> 00:51:18.680
Two fruit cocktails, two trout with au gratin potatoes,

00:51:20.040 --> 00:51:22.600
two orders of salad, a thousand-dollar dressing.

00:51:22.880 --> 00:51:23.220
Got that?

00:51:23.490 --> 00:51:23.990
Yes, sir.

00:51:24.860 --> 00:51:25.820
We'll order dessert later.

00:51:26.320 --> 00:51:26.740
Yes, sir.

00:51:30.250 --> 00:51:31.430
What have you been living, in a barrel?

00:51:32.000 --> 00:51:33.120
I live in San Mero.

00:51:35.530 --> 00:51:36.310
You know, it's kind of funny.

00:51:37.230 --> 00:51:39.030
For a minute, I thought I was back in New Guinea again.

00:51:39.740 --> 00:51:40.900
Only in New Guinea, they're darker.

00:51:41.680 --> 00:51:42.240
Who is?

00:51:42.950 --> 00:51:43.270
Girls.

00:51:44.460 --> 00:51:45.480
You like them darker?

00:51:48.240 --> 00:51:50.100
If you're going to laugh at me, I'll go away.

00:51:51.790 --> 00:51:52.850
Nobody's laughing at you.

00:51:53.920 --> 00:51:54.740
What a goon.

00:52:10.060 --> 00:52:13.060
A lot of different kinds of fruit, all chopped up.

00:52:13.700 --> 00:52:14.540
Go ahead, eat it. It's good.

00:52:18.590 --> 00:52:25.940
That smells very good. That's to keep it cold. That's very nice.

00:52:27.810 --> 00:52:29.750
Some mellow, ice is very hard to get.

00:52:30.640 --> 00:52:33.660
We put everything down the well by string, and it...

00:52:33.660 --> 00:52:44.340
I must talk to you, Mr. Gagan. It's very important, and I've only got a few minutes.

00:52:45.240 --> 00:52:46.080
Rags coming down.

00:52:46.920 --> 00:52:49.340
You said you put things down the well with the string, huh?

00:52:49.720 --> 00:52:50.940
Please, couldn't we go to another table?

00:52:51.160 --> 00:52:53.150
No, we couldn't. Can't you see we're having lunch?

00:52:53.700 --> 00:52:56.450
But I must talk to you alone. I'm terribly sorry.

00:52:58.080 --> 00:52:59.980
Please, Mr. Gagan, I'm only asking three minutes.

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:02.880
but they're very important minutes for both of us.

00:53:04.890 --> 00:53:08.060
Okay. You go on over and sit at another table.

00:53:08.460 --> 00:53:09.800
Over there. I'll call you.

00:53:10.350 --> 00:53:11.890
You will excuse us for a moment, won't you?

00:53:16.820 --> 00:53:17.680
It's on your mind.

00:53:18.530 --> 00:53:20.050
Frank just told me what you're doing,

00:53:20.250 --> 00:53:22.050
and I rushed right down here hoping to find you.

00:53:23.160 --> 00:53:24.040
You don't know me.

00:53:24.410 --> 00:53:26.250
You have no reason to believe anything I say,

00:53:26.980 --> 00:53:28.620
but you can't lose anything by listening.

00:53:30.220 --> 00:53:32.580
I'm listening. He's very clever, Frankie.

00:53:33.250 --> 00:53:35.450
He's seen to it that I have everything except money.

00:53:35.900 --> 00:53:41.620
But I could get out with money. I know what you're thinking.

00:53:42.230 --> 00:53:44.290
What's she up to? Why do I even listen to her?

00:53:44.740 --> 00:53:45.680
You said it, sister.

00:53:46.210 --> 00:53:48.970
You're such a fool, asking for only 30,000.

00:53:49.330 --> 00:53:51.130
Do you know what he'd ask for in your place?

00:53:51.450 --> 00:53:52.890
A million and gotten it.

00:53:53.050 --> 00:53:55.370
If you'll let me do it, I'll get you twice as much.

00:53:55.720 --> 00:53:56.920
And get what I want, too.

00:53:57.980 --> 00:53:59.790
How? Will you let me?

00:54:00.320 --> 00:54:01.020
I asked you, how?

00:54:01.420 --> 00:54:02.440
Don't give him the check.

00:54:02.910 --> 00:54:05.390
Give it to a lawyer in Tulsa or any place else,

00:54:05.510 --> 00:54:07.490
New York, Chicago, some honest lawyer.

00:54:08.060 --> 00:54:11.040
Put it in a sealed envelope and pay him $1,000 fee.

00:54:11.380 --> 00:54:14.550
And tell him that if anything happens to either you or me,

00:54:14.830 --> 00:54:16.950
he's to send the envelope to the FBI.

00:54:17.450 --> 00:54:19.110
Then you go to Frank and tell him what you've done

00:54:19.110 --> 00:54:20.830
and ask for $100,000.

00:54:21.180 --> 00:54:23.520
And when that's gone, you ask for another $100,000.

00:54:23.660 --> 00:54:26.300
And we become sort of partners with Frankie.

00:54:27.430 --> 00:54:29.970
I've learned this sort of high finance from Frankie and...

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:35.490
himself too rich for me but don't you see it's more than the money it's the only way you can keep

00:54:35.490 --> 00:54:41.040
alive you don't think frank's gonna let you enjoy it even if he gives it to you i'll enjoy it all

00:54:41.040 --> 00:54:48.380
right i know you're not afraid but why not get more it's so simple no i don't play but why i don't

00:54:48.380 --> 00:54:54.500
trust that lawyer the one who eclipses for a grand i said we'd find an honest one hugo buys

00:54:54.500 --> 00:54:59.670
them all even the honest ones but he won't know who he is you'll know

00:55:01.760 --> 00:55:06.990
Oh, I see. And, of course, you can't trust me.

00:55:07.920 --> 00:55:12.130
Right. Then do it yourself. I'll trust you.

00:55:13.770 --> 00:55:17.180
Too many angles. Please, it's tremendous if you do it right.

00:55:17.440 --> 00:55:21.120
He has millions. You're smart cookie, aren't you?

00:55:23.050 --> 00:55:26.340
I'll do it my way. But it's stupid. So stupid.

00:55:27.240 --> 00:55:29.790
Maybe. I found out something, though.

00:55:30.600 --> 00:55:32.500
There are a lot of people in this world smarter than me,

00:55:33.140 --> 00:55:36.220
and they aren't sitting up nice figuring out how to help me either.

00:55:37.080 --> 00:55:40.010
But I'll buy you a drink. What do you have?

00:55:43.490 --> 00:55:44.410
Nothing, thank you.

00:55:48.100 --> 00:55:57.160
Hey, come on back. What's your name?

00:55:58.400 --> 00:55:58.760
Peeler.

00:55:59.760 --> 00:55:59.980
Peeler?

00:56:00.700 --> 00:56:03.420
Peela, I want you to meet Miss Marjorie Lundin.

00:56:03.860 --> 00:56:07.410
How do you do? I'm terribly sorry about intruding like this.

00:56:10.420 --> 00:56:12.580
This must be a dull town after the fiesta.

00:56:14.070 --> 00:56:15.850
Dusty and hot and full of flies.

00:56:17.020 --> 00:56:18.260
I'm glad I don't live here.

00:56:18.780 --> 00:56:21.520
Because I like bright lights and night spots and lots of people.

00:56:22.670 --> 00:56:24.170
I'm afraid I wasn't cut out for it.

00:56:27.030 --> 00:56:27.930
I'll try and see you later.

00:56:28.680 --> 00:56:29.860
Please think of what I told you.

00:56:30.920 --> 00:56:31.960
It was nice meeting you.

00:56:32.060 --> 00:56:41.320
If you make you feel bad, I guess you're not used to her kind of ladies.

00:56:43.320 --> 00:56:44.460
She's very beautiful.

00:56:45.000 --> 00:56:46.920
Yeah, they usually are.

00:56:48.340 --> 00:56:51.170
She has very nice clothes and diamonds.

00:56:51.690 --> 00:56:54.320
Diamonds and a dead fish where her heart ought to be.

00:56:55.360 --> 00:56:56.320
I know a lot of them babies.

00:56:56.860 --> 00:56:57.900
She's not a baby.

00:56:58.600 --> 00:56:59.960
Babies is what you call dames.

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:05.220
do you understand that no you understand what a human being is yes well they're not human beings

00:57:05.220 --> 00:57:10.940
they're dead fish with a lot of perfume on them you touch them and you always get stung you always

00:57:10.940 --> 00:57:22.830
lose you do not like no my friend maria is like that jose bought her a new pair of shoes and she

00:57:22.830 --> 00:57:26.190
wouldn't wear them in front of him but tonight at the dance she's gonna wear them in front of other

00:57:26.190 --> 00:57:29.970
men and i told that she shouldn't be like that because he's a boy and four and

00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:41.400
She should wear them for him because a man doesn't like for a girl always to go barefoot go on eat your lunch

00:57:41.400 --> 00:57:45.000
I got some business. I got it would tend to

00:58:10.330 --> 00:58:15.420
Thank you.

01:00:06.620 --> 01:00:07.920
Sounds like the fiestas started.

01:00:08.380 --> 01:00:09.280
Well, not too late.

01:00:09.770 --> 01:00:11.670
They're taking Olses over to the plaza for the big burning.

01:00:12.020 --> 01:00:13.000
We're still in plenty of time.

01:00:13.580 --> 01:00:14.380
Who ordered scoff?

01:00:14.540 --> 01:00:14.980
I did.

01:00:15.530 --> 01:00:16.330
There's not much there.

01:00:16.700 --> 01:00:17.480
Not very hungry.

01:00:18.320 --> 01:00:19.360
Bring the wine now, will you?

01:00:19.610 --> 01:00:20.050
Yes, sir.

01:00:20.910 --> 01:00:24.420
How is everything, Mr. Hughville?

01:00:24.780 --> 01:00:25.220
What's that?

01:00:27.080 --> 01:00:28.260
Well, who's here?

01:00:28.670 --> 01:00:29.650
Must be seven o'clock.

01:00:30.090 --> 01:00:30.630
On the nose?

01:00:30.790 --> 01:00:32.050
Nothing like being on time.

01:00:32.660 --> 01:00:33.740
I said, how is everything?

01:00:34.290 --> 01:00:36.900
Oh, I'll have to hang around for a few minutes.

01:00:37.060 --> 01:00:38.640
The bank messenger's coming from Tulsa.

01:00:39.160 --> 01:00:40.260
You all set with your end of it?

01:00:40.640 --> 01:00:40.860
Yeah.

01:00:43.280 --> 01:00:44.880
He's scared stiff, I'm gonna stand him up.

01:00:46.000 --> 01:00:47.520
Messenger phone, he'd be a little late.

01:00:47.640 --> 01:00:48.660
Why don't you wait over at the bar?

01:00:48.780 --> 01:00:49.520
I'll let you know when he comes.

01:00:49.760 --> 01:00:50.740
Why wait at the bar?

01:00:50.900 --> 01:00:51.640
Pull up a chair.

01:00:51.880 --> 01:00:52.620
There's plenty of room.

01:00:52.720 --> 01:00:54.260
I prefer Mr. Gagan at the bar.

01:00:54.560 --> 01:00:55.760
Don't be silly, Frank.

01:00:57.160 --> 01:00:58.280
I feel like dancing.

01:00:58.600 --> 01:00:59.780
After all, it is a fiesta.

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:01.260
Your squab will get cold.

01:01:01.660 --> 01:01:03.300
Keep it warm for me, will you, Frank?

01:01:04.510 --> 01:01:04.930
Mine?

01:01:11.840 --> 01:01:13.760
Dancing will be better than sitting at the bar.

01:01:15.260 --> 01:01:16.980
I've been furious at you all day.

01:01:17.280 --> 01:01:19.980
You've cost me $50,000 by your bullheadedness.

01:01:20.300 --> 01:01:22.520
$50,000 and freedom and fun.

01:01:25.100 --> 01:01:27.000
I don't know why I feel this way about you.

01:01:27.640 --> 01:01:29.260
Oh, I'm not making a pass at you.

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:30.880
Just being stupid.

01:01:32.380 --> 01:01:33.120
What's on your mind?

01:01:33.750 --> 01:01:34.010
You?

01:01:34.170 --> 01:01:36.700
What are we waiting for?

01:01:37.620 --> 01:01:38.420
He's watching us.

01:01:38.620 --> 01:01:39.420
I'm afraid to talk.

01:01:40.520 --> 01:01:45.540
He isn't going to give you the money.

01:01:47.300 --> 01:01:47.700
No?

01:01:48.680 --> 01:01:50.600
He's figured out one of his typical tricks.

01:01:51.420 --> 01:01:51.640
What?

01:01:52.060 --> 01:01:53.580
Is he watching us?

01:01:55.340 --> 01:01:55.600
No.

01:02:02.880 --> 01:02:19.380
Have you got a cigarette? I shouldn't be telling you this.

01:02:20.000 --> 01:02:22.100
You certainly haven't done anything to deserve it.

01:02:23.420 --> 01:02:26.370
But there isn't any bank messenger coming. There's someone else.

01:02:27.060 --> 01:02:28.430
Who? I don't know.

01:02:30.030 --> 01:02:51.780
Sorry, I know you.

01:02:52.450 --> 01:02:53.740
I don't know. Do you?

01:02:54.240 --> 01:02:55.860
Everyone knows everyone on Fiesta night.

01:02:56.820 --> 01:02:57.260
Are you dancing?

01:02:57.830 --> 01:02:58.750
Not so you'd notice.

01:02:59.160 --> 01:02:59.860
Where's Gagin?

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:04.170
He stopped to talk to someone. It's a good orchestra, isn't it? Dance?

01:03:04.570 --> 01:03:05.510
Some other time.

01:03:06.130 --> 01:03:06.350
What?

01:03:20.900 --> 01:03:21.500
No bourbon.

01:03:22.460 --> 01:03:23.180
Double bourbon.

01:03:23.650 --> 01:03:23.950
Yes, sir.

01:03:25.340 --> 01:03:27.020
Well, I should have had a steak.

01:03:37.580 --> 01:03:40.780
There's a couple of your friends outside. You better go have a look.

01:03:41.830 --> 01:03:42.350
What friends?

01:03:42.890 --> 01:03:45.410
So they aren't your friends, but you ought to have a look anyway.

01:03:46.140 --> 01:03:49.540
You ought to know better than to send a couple of knife fighters against Gagin.

01:03:49.820 --> 01:03:51.140
I don't know anything about Gagin.

01:03:51.450 --> 01:03:54.390
Maybe you don't, but your friends don't look so good out there.

01:03:55.150 --> 01:03:57.610
Mr. Retz, I'm having my dinner. You're giving me indigestion.

01:03:58.020 --> 01:03:59.740
I don't care what kind of a badge you're wearing.

01:04:00.570 --> 01:04:02.670
Saw, ain't you? Glad to see it.

01:04:03.010 --> 01:04:05.930
You wouldn't be saw if you got what you wanted from Gagin.

01:04:06.530 --> 01:04:08.940
I'm grateful to you, Mr. Hugo. Thanks.

01:04:11.800 --> 01:04:13.720
Take Miss Santoya to the fiesta, will you, Jim?

01:04:14.080 --> 01:04:16.860
Come along, my dear. I'll be at the hotel.

01:04:17.140 --> 01:04:17.660
Call you there.

01:04:19.580 --> 01:04:23.210
What happened?

01:04:23.850 --> 01:04:25.280
They got him. I saw him.

01:04:25.320 --> 01:04:28.860
But he got away. Take her to the fiesta. Keep your eyes open for him.

01:04:28.960 --> 01:04:29.980
He's crawling around somewhere.

01:04:30.500 --> 01:04:31.730
Bring him back to the hotel.

01:04:32.280 --> 01:04:33.140
What about the cops?

01:04:33.360 --> 01:04:33.920
What about them?

01:04:36.080 --> 01:04:36.680
I'm worried.

01:04:37.910 --> 01:04:39.130
I'm not worried about a thing.

01:04:49.990 --> 01:04:50.470
Who are you?

01:04:51.420 --> 01:04:52.160
I phoned you.

01:04:53.610 --> 01:04:54.390
I heard you were in town.

01:04:54.490 --> 01:04:54.850
Where are they?

01:04:55.110 --> 01:04:55.770
Right over here.

01:05:06.620 --> 01:05:07.600
Broke this baby's arm.

01:05:08.830 --> 01:05:10.810
This one looks a little dead. Couldn't be deader.

01:05:11.400 --> 01:05:13.960
Neat job. Hey, here's a lot of blood.

01:05:14.520 --> 01:05:15.800
This character's missing his knife.

01:05:16.360 --> 01:05:17.340
Must have left it in the other guy.

01:05:17.460 --> 01:05:18.260
If he had a knife.

01:05:18.570 --> 01:05:20.840
Winneke, he always carried a knife.

01:05:21.560 --> 01:05:23.680
Pretty bad boy, and plenty tough, too.

01:05:24.000 --> 01:05:25.060
That guy can't be far.

01:05:25.800 --> 01:05:27.580
Maybe we can run him down with all that blood out of him.

01:05:28.300 --> 01:05:29.100
Let's look in the cars.

01:06:11.840 --> 01:06:14.520
Get the knife out.

01:06:24.910 --> 01:06:26.150
I will stop the bleeding.

01:06:38.380 --> 01:06:43.110
Tyler, Tyler.

01:06:49.810 --> 01:06:50.670
Release out there.

01:06:52.880 --> 01:06:53.400
Be safe.

01:06:54.500 --> 01:06:55.200
Bleeding stopped.

01:06:57.210 --> 01:06:57.410
Yes.

01:07:02.010 --> 01:07:02.870
Let me get out of here.

01:07:19.950 --> 01:07:20.490
What's that?

01:07:21.210 --> 01:07:21.910
The V.S. Duck.

01:07:24.560 --> 01:07:27.790
Look slow. Keep in the dark.

01:07:30.320 --> 01:07:30.880
Does it hurt?

01:07:31.540 --> 01:07:32.680
Yeah, it hurts.

01:08:05.690 --> 01:08:07.630
My friend, how is it?

01:08:08.630 --> 01:08:09.850
Can you help?

01:08:10.330 --> 01:08:11.170
I'll fix you.

01:08:12.620 --> 01:08:16.910
What kind of hurt?

01:08:18.600 --> 01:08:20.780
Knife. Where? In the back.

01:08:21.680 --> 01:08:24.260
Knife is good. It's more easy to fix.

01:08:24.800 --> 01:08:26.100
I got knife three times.

01:08:26.820 --> 01:08:29.060
When you're young, everybody sticks knife in you.

01:08:30.120 --> 01:08:34.100
Lie still, take big drink, and couldn't assume you're more better than the quality.

01:08:34.340 --> 01:08:35.020
Sit down in here.

01:08:36.070 --> 01:08:36.970
Oh, hold his head.

01:08:37.330 --> 01:08:43.160
You take big drink, eh?

01:08:48.980 --> 01:08:49.840
Drink long time.

01:08:54.210 --> 01:08:54.650
Stimmer.

01:08:57.290 --> 01:08:58.390
Hey, you fix this, eh?

01:08:58.990 --> 01:08:59.210
See.

01:09:00.350 --> 01:09:04.390
That's a good kid. I leave it alone, but I make more tighter.

01:09:04.710 --> 01:09:17.060
You feel now, mi amigo? Sure, sure.

01:09:21.510 --> 01:09:24.640
Somebody else was hurt? Yes.

01:09:26.230 --> 01:09:28.510
One is dead.

01:09:31.120 --> 01:09:33.200
Good. Buena, buena, buena.

01:09:35.990 --> 01:09:39.370
Your coat is pretty bad. I don't think we can fix him.

01:09:41.480 --> 01:09:46.610
Give me the wallet, the inside pocket.

01:09:46.830 --> 01:09:52.430
Ah, it's here, all right.

01:09:53.920 --> 01:09:54.400
My gun.

01:09:55.940 --> 01:09:57.520
No, no, she's gone, it's gone.

01:09:57.800 --> 01:09:59.980
Uh, great hand pocket.

01:10:02.650 --> 01:10:06.500
No gun, mi amigo. You don't need gun. You've got poncho now.

01:10:06.680 --> 01:10:11.430
It'll be all right. Sure.

01:10:12.020 --> 01:10:13.840
It'll be all right in a few minutes.

01:10:14.180 --> 01:10:20.180
Sure, sure.

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:53.700
like them two guys they look bad what they come to punch you for after him quick help me we hide him

01:11:06.750 --> 01:11:08.550
No, no, no, no, cleaners, stay on.

01:11:09.990 --> 01:11:11.050
Everybody free ride.

01:12:07.960 --> 01:12:08.500
You wanna get on?

01:12:09.110 --> 01:12:10.870
10 centavos, 10 cents.

01:12:11.510 --> 01:12:12.710
Next ride right away.

01:12:13.810 --> 01:12:14.510
Come over here.

01:12:14.650 --> 01:12:16.580
What do you want?

01:12:17.370 --> 01:12:18.570
I said come over here.

01:12:19.940 --> 01:12:21.220
What's the matter, you looking for something?

01:12:21.980 --> 01:12:23.480
Looking for a guy named Pancho.

01:12:24.070 --> 01:12:25.490
You find him, that's me.

01:12:26.660 --> 01:12:27.480
Where's Gagin?

01:12:28.670 --> 01:12:29.090
Gagin?

01:12:30.250 --> 01:12:33.800
Who's he? Tell me you met in a saloon last night.

01:12:34.280 --> 01:12:36.620
Oh, him. He's gigging.

01:12:37.430 --> 01:12:38.770
He don't told me his name.

01:12:39.270 --> 01:12:39.930
Where is he?

01:12:40.820 --> 01:12:42.880
Oh, I should know. Why you ask Poncho?

01:12:43.120 --> 01:12:44.000
I don't know nothing.

01:12:44.560 --> 01:12:45.780
Where'd you take him last night?

01:12:46.770 --> 01:12:47.930
Last night I'm drunk.

01:12:48.550 --> 01:12:50.710
All I know is I wake up, I'm still drunk.

01:12:51.460 --> 01:12:52.500
What do you fellas want?

01:13:00.410 --> 01:13:06.680
I know nothing.

01:13:08.010 --> 01:13:19.140
I know, I'll tell you.

01:13:27.340 --> 01:13:27.740
Lion.

01:13:28.700 --> 01:13:29.260
Where is he?

01:13:38.070 --> 01:13:42.130
He's holding out not that fat slob he don't know from nothing

01:14:28.000 --> 01:14:29.320
is just tell me your name.

01:14:30.830 --> 01:14:32.810
Pleased to know you, Mr. Gagin.

01:14:33.130 --> 01:14:36.000
They want to know, where is Gagin?

01:14:36.640 --> 01:14:37.280
I don't know.

01:14:37.840 --> 01:14:39.480
Boom in the nose, I don't know.

01:14:40.320 --> 01:14:41.840
Boom in the mouth, I don't know.

01:14:42.770 --> 01:14:44.680
I fall down, but I don't know.

01:14:45.620 --> 01:14:47.940
I told you, Pancho, a very proud man.

01:14:50.960 --> 01:14:52.120
Got to cut you in, Pancho.

01:14:52.850 --> 01:14:53.790
Cut me in?

01:14:53.930 --> 01:14:54.850
And what, mi amigo?

01:14:56.040 --> 01:14:56.700
Five grand.

01:14:57.820 --> 01:14:58.180
Grand?

01:15:00.160 --> 01:15:00.980
5,000 bucks.

01:15:01.630 --> 01:15:02.870
You got that much money.

01:15:04.720 --> 01:15:05.320
I'm going to get it.

01:15:05.770 --> 01:15:08.450
Yeah, lots of people going to get lots of things, but they don't.

01:15:09.230 --> 01:15:10.350
You ain't got it yet, huh?

01:15:10.960 --> 01:15:11.480
Not yet.

01:15:13.160 --> 01:15:13.800
I'm going to get it.

01:15:14.880 --> 01:15:16.000
We've got to get going.

01:15:16.200 --> 01:15:16.860
No, no, not now.

01:15:16.940 --> 01:15:17.420
You're sick.

01:15:18.420 --> 01:15:20.560
I'm not going to get any better if those guys come back.

01:15:20.740 --> 01:15:21.280
He's right.

01:15:21.400 --> 01:15:22.120
He goes away.

01:15:22.520 --> 01:15:23.400
Maybe they come back.

01:15:23.700 --> 01:15:24.580
Fiesta come here.

01:15:24.760 --> 01:15:25.420
Dancers here.

01:15:25.640 --> 01:15:27.220
Somebody see him, they find him.

01:15:27.360 --> 01:15:28.520
Yeah, they're not going to stop looking.

01:15:30.480 --> 01:15:32.280
I'll be all right as soon as I get my punch back.

01:15:32.960 --> 01:15:34.300
We will go to San Melo.

01:15:35.310 --> 01:15:35.870
Where's that?

01:15:36.230 --> 01:15:37.130
Two hours by bus.

01:15:38.040 --> 01:15:39.080
Are you sure there's a bus?

01:15:39.410 --> 01:15:40.870
Si, he leaves at 10 o'clock.

01:15:41.090 --> 01:15:44.920
We got an hour and a half to wait.

01:15:46.040 --> 01:15:47.240
Can't wait in that bus station.

01:15:47.590 --> 01:15:49.050
You go to the three violators.

01:15:49.750 --> 01:15:50.890
You're Pancho's friend.

01:15:51.210 --> 01:15:51.690
They remember.

01:15:52.220 --> 01:15:53.640
Here, take him, hurry, quick.

01:15:54.400 --> 01:15:55.380
Adios, mi amigo.

01:15:56.020 --> 01:15:59.930
Hey, this burns so sober.

01:16:00.470 --> 01:16:01.930
God of bad luck.

01:16:04.790 --> 01:16:06.730
Man, they don't burn him hour ago.

01:16:08.030 --> 01:16:08.610
Hurry.

01:16:47.790 --> 01:16:48.730
I'm a good friend of Pancho.

01:16:49.230 --> 01:16:50.350
Tio Vivo Pancho.

01:16:50.470 --> 01:16:51.610
Ah, a good friend.

01:16:51.770 --> 01:16:52.730
I remember the night.

01:16:52.930 --> 01:16:53.460
Is he?

01:16:53.660 --> 01:16:54.440
Yes, he's sick.

01:16:55.100 --> 01:16:56.280
Do you not feel good, señor?

01:16:56.760 --> 01:16:57.380
The sombrero.

01:16:57.730 --> 01:16:58.270
It's mine.

01:16:58.530 --> 01:16:59.290
I want to borrow it.

01:16:59.450 --> 01:16:59.790
How much?

01:17:00.120 --> 01:17:03.050
Nada, nada. You'll bring it back some time.

01:17:03.980 --> 01:17:17.060
Take him back there. Nobody see you, right?

01:17:17.840 --> 01:17:17.960
Si.

01:17:18.560 --> 01:17:20.010
Want your help? Si.

01:17:20.130 --> 01:17:21.490
How is he? He's all right.

01:17:55.560 --> 01:17:57.750
We will stay here. Then we will go to the bus.

01:17:57.990 --> 01:17:58.710
Yes, yes, that's fine.

01:18:00.220 --> 01:18:02.890
If there's no one comes, I'll tell you.

01:18:03.050 --> 01:18:06.830
How do you feel now?

01:18:07.070 --> 01:18:16.420
I know what's going on.

01:18:17.640 --> 01:18:19.850
I know. They tried to kill you.

01:18:19.970 --> 01:18:23.640
You want to know why?

01:18:24.710 --> 01:18:25.670
Because they are bad.

01:18:28.130 --> 01:18:29.070
And I'm good, huh?

01:18:30.510 --> 01:18:32.600
Yes, I will take care of you.

01:18:32.860 --> 01:18:38.310
He's just like Shorty.

01:18:39.910 --> 01:18:40.450
No brain.

01:18:41.990 --> 01:18:42.390
Don't talk.

01:18:44.410 --> 01:18:45.190
It hurts better now.

01:18:47.830 --> 01:18:48.630
It's hot in me.

01:18:51.300 --> 01:18:53.580
Hot in the jungle too.

01:18:56.420 --> 01:18:57.500
Rain turns to steam.

01:18:58.280 --> 01:18:59.240
Eve, don't go to sleep.

01:19:01.080 --> 01:19:01.540
Okay.

01:19:02.960 --> 01:19:10.990
Okay, shorty, except for you.

01:19:24.560 --> 01:19:27.060
Put that in your shirt.

01:19:33.580 --> 01:19:37.550
Hang on to it. Don't let nobody touch it.

01:19:39.790 --> 01:19:40.150
Nobody.

01:19:41.450 --> 01:19:41.730
Nobody.

01:19:43.360 --> 01:19:57.920
A un desconocido.

01:20:53.450 --> 01:20:56.210
They're coming.

01:22:25.790 --> 01:22:28.010
Next bus will leave till 10 o'clock.

01:22:30.090 --> 01:22:32.290
Oh, he's gone down the street to watch the fiesta.

01:24:04.190 --> 01:24:07.700
Uh, find a hotel.

01:24:08.180 --> 01:24:08.540
What?

01:24:10.720 --> 01:24:11.160
Hotel.

01:24:12.270 --> 01:24:13.330
Oh, they're there, senor.

01:24:30.730 --> 01:24:31.610
Didn't order a drink.

01:24:32.890 --> 01:24:34.030
Never mind, leave it there.

01:24:37.260 --> 01:24:37.580
Window.

01:24:38.480 --> 01:24:38.920
Yes, sir.

01:24:42.990 --> 01:24:43.390
Better.

01:24:48.670 --> 01:24:49.070
I'll get it.

01:24:53.200 --> 01:24:55.480
Jeff, I can't hear you.

01:24:57.250 --> 01:24:57.510
Yeah?

01:24:58.850 --> 01:24:59.250
They did...

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:02.420
What's the matter with you? Don't call me unless you've got something to tell me.

01:25:15.090 --> 01:25:15.810
Where did he go?

01:25:16.160 --> 01:25:17.700
The man with his blood in his hand?

01:25:17.900 --> 01:25:18.920
Yes. He went there.

01:27:10.010 --> 01:27:11.870
Mr. Gagin, please.

01:27:27.300 --> 01:27:27.520
Which?

01:27:30.920 --> 01:27:34.510
Which one of you is Frank Hugo?

01:27:36.800 --> 01:27:40.370
I'm Hugo. Put that thing away, don't you see? He's out on his feet.

01:27:41.730 --> 01:27:42.910
See if anyone else is with him.

01:27:52.290 --> 01:27:52.590
Buddy.

01:27:55.560 --> 01:27:56.640
Bring him in and shut the door.

01:28:02.400 --> 01:28:14.320
Sit him down. Who's the girl? What's the matter with him?

01:28:15.140 --> 01:28:17.260
Do not remember. He's hurt.

01:28:17.780 --> 01:28:25.900
Better see if he has a gun. What did you want to talk to me about?

01:28:30.030 --> 01:28:30.450
Shorty.

01:28:30.980 --> 01:28:32.440
Yeah, you're his pal.

01:28:36.310 --> 01:28:37.010
I've got Shorty.

01:28:37.480 --> 01:28:38.500
But I was pretty dumb.

01:28:40.080 --> 01:28:41.360
I didn't get what I was after.

01:28:43.380 --> 01:28:44.180
What was I after?

01:28:52.280 --> 01:28:52.440
Tech.

01:28:53.170 --> 01:28:54.130
You want to sell it to me.

01:28:55.160 --> 01:28:56.200
How much do you want for it?

01:29:01.560 --> 01:29:02.340
30 grand.

01:29:02.720 --> 01:29:04.200
It's a deal. I'll pay it in cash.

01:29:05.160 --> 01:29:06.080
You got the check with you?

01:29:11.020 --> 01:29:11.340
Money.

01:29:11.580 --> 01:29:12.620
Right here in my hand.

01:29:25.310 --> 01:29:25.950
Can't you find it?

01:29:31.470 --> 01:29:40.800
There's no check in here. What did you do with it? Come on. Where is it? What did you do with it? I don't know

01:29:40.800 --> 01:29:45.920
What do you know about it? I don't know nothing. Where'd you pick him up?

01:29:46.660 --> 01:29:52.930
Until Vivo. He was hurt. He came there. Where'd he go then? I don't know. You don't know. You were with him?

01:29:52.970 --> 01:29:59.850
What were you doing with him? He's sick. Please, he's sick. Gagan. Wake up, Gagan.

01:30:01.340 --> 01:30:04.260
I got the money right here. Now, where's the check?

01:30:05.780 --> 01:30:07.900
Try and think. The check. Shorty's check.

01:30:08.190 --> 01:30:09.050
What did you do with it?

01:30:12.930 --> 01:30:15.320
I want to see Frank Hugo.

01:30:15.680 --> 01:30:17.360
You cannot take him away now.

01:30:17.820 --> 01:30:29.530
Get him a drink. That's his stuff.

01:30:31.660 --> 01:30:35.210
You feel better now, don't you? You remember where the check is.

01:30:35.990 --> 01:30:38.370
You hid it someplace because you were afraid you wouldn't get the money.

01:30:39.060 --> 01:30:40.480
But here's the money. Now, where's the check?

01:30:45.180 --> 01:30:45.720
I don't know.

01:30:45.900 --> 01:30:49.090
Sure you do. You put it someplace. Now, where did you put it?

01:30:52.190 --> 01:30:52.630
I don't remember.

01:30:52.890 --> 01:30:55.120
You're gonna remember. It was in your wallet.

01:30:58.300 --> 01:30:59.970
Yeah, you took it out.

01:31:04.220 --> 01:31:06.200
He took it out. Where did you put it?

01:31:09.250 --> 01:31:09.950
I don't remember.

01:31:12.700 --> 01:31:13.800
Yeah, I can help him remember.

01:31:14.080 --> 01:31:15.040
Yeah, go ahead.

01:31:19.700 --> 01:31:20.080
Where is it?

01:31:24.480 --> 01:31:25.560
Oh, he lost it.

01:31:25.710 --> 01:31:26.990
He lost it, huh? Where'd he lose it?

01:31:27.360 --> 01:31:27.900
I don't know.

01:31:28.160 --> 01:31:29.340
Then how do you know he lost it?

01:31:30.160 --> 01:31:31.520
Maybe she'll talk for you, Tommy.

01:31:39.750 --> 01:31:41.970
Where is it? Come on, you know where it is.

01:31:42.150 --> 01:31:43.210
She don't know where it is, boss.

01:31:43.430 --> 01:31:45.390
She knows, all right. Go on, keep it up.

01:31:49.560 --> 01:31:51.580
Why don't you help me, Mr. Hugosa?

01:31:52.140 --> 01:31:54.120
You're the one who knows how to treat a lady.

01:31:54.970 --> 01:31:55.810
Who let you in?

01:31:57.200 --> 01:31:58.780
Maybe you don't like knocking on doors.

01:32:00.090 --> 01:32:03.760
Maybe you like this guy over here. His line is blackmailed.

01:32:04.670 --> 01:32:08.400
One of these haywire veterans trying to put the bite on me for 30 grand.

01:32:08.940 --> 01:32:10.440
What's your bite, mister? Is it...

01:32:19.330 --> 01:32:23.790
Giggin. Giggin. Get up, boy. Get over there.

01:32:23.930 --> 01:32:29.520
Pick up, son.

01:32:31.120 --> 01:32:33.320
It's all right, miss. You can come over here now.

01:32:33.910 --> 01:32:38.280
It's all right. I've been following you, Gagan, ever since you left the merry-go-round.

01:32:38.940 --> 01:32:43.700
Sorry to use you as bait, but I wanted to be in on it when he tried to wrangle that check out of you.

01:32:44.520 --> 01:32:46.420
Stay behind me, son. Stay behind me.

01:32:47.600 --> 01:32:48.600
Need it bad for evidence?

01:32:49.220 --> 01:32:51.620
Could have got it, too, if I waited another five minutes.

01:32:52.470 --> 01:32:53.990
But I guess I just couldn't wait.

01:32:54.650 --> 01:32:56.510
Ain't nice seeing folks get pushed around.

01:32:57.370 --> 01:32:59.400
We're in bad company here. Come on.

01:32:59.610 --> 01:32:59.930
Go ahead.

01:33:00.440 --> 01:33:02.140
Be a sucker. Walk out on yourself.

01:33:02.790 --> 01:33:05.810
Come here to pick up some easy money, just as it's in your pocket, you walk out.

01:33:06.820 --> 01:33:10.060
This guy makes me laugh. His idea of big money.

01:33:10.840 --> 01:33:13.440
He's got me right where it hurts, and all he asks for is 30 grand.

01:33:14.280 --> 01:33:17.960
Guys like you work all their lives, breaking their backs, trying to earn meat and potatoes.

01:33:18.680 --> 01:33:21.460
You end up borrowing enough money to buy a hole in the ground to get buried in.

01:33:22.220 --> 01:33:24.660
Then when you get a chance to make some real scratch, what do you do?

01:33:25.170 --> 01:33:27.670
Mice like you and Shorty. You ask for peanuts.

01:33:28.570 --> 01:33:29.910
You know what's gonna happen when you get out.

01:33:30.000 --> 01:33:33.450
He's going to give you a lot of gas about duty and honor.

01:33:34.200 --> 01:33:37.860
Fill you with fancy words like responsibility, patriotism.

01:33:38.680 --> 01:33:39.960
That's how he's going to get that check.

01:33:40.640 --> 01:33:42.120
And what are you going to have? Nothing.

01:33:42.890 --> 01:33:45.770
Sure, maybe I'll get sent to the pen a lot of bucks that'll put in your pocket.

01:33:46.560 --> 01:33:49.500
I don't know why I talk to a lug like you. Small fry.

01:33:49.990 --> 01:33:52.910
All your life you waste time worrying about small fry things.

01:33:53.420 --> 01:33:56.240
About a job, about a two-buck raise, about getting a pension.

01:33:57.110 --> 01:33:59.980
Why don't you ask for 300 grand? 300 thou-

01:34:01.290 --> 01:34:02.890
It'll set you up for the rest of your life.

01:34:08.840 --> 01:34:09.500
Give me that check.

01:34:19.170 --> 01:34:20.110
Now you're talking.

01:34:20.860 --> 01:34:22.080
He can't hear you, Gagan.

01:34:22.740 --> 01:34:23.980
His tin ear is busted.

01:34:27.270 --> 01:34:28.290
Maybe he can hear this.

01:34:41.320 --> 01:34:42.440
I like to eat with my hands.

01:34:42.600 --> 01:34:44.920
It gets me closer to the food.

01:34:47.530 --> 01:34:49.380
What's the matter? Eggs cold?

01:34:50.160 --> 01:34:52.490
Coffee stale? Toast burn?

01:34:53.420 --> 01:34:54.340
I'm not hungry.

01:34:55.560 --> 01:34:57.600
Funny thing, every time I fret, I can't eat.

01:34:58.620 --> 01:34:59.660
What makes you think I'm fretting?

01:35:00.250 --> 01:35:02.150
Two bucks worth of breakfast going to pot.

01:35:03.340 --> 01:35:05.680
But it ain't the five grand you promised Pancho, is it?

01:35:05.980 --> 01:35:08.470
No. He never expected to get that anyway.

01:35:09.150 --> 01:35:12.170
Couldn't be that 300,000 you turned down the other night.

01:35:13.200 --> 01:35:15.380
Fat chance I'd have of collecting that with you around.

01:35:16.950 --> 01:35:17.790
Is it the kid?

01:35:19.870 --> 01:35:20.450
What kid?

01:35:21.360 --> 01:35:22.880
A little mouse with the big eyes.

01:35:23.790 --> 01:35:25.470
You wouldn't be fretting about her now, would you?

01:35:26.130 --> 01:35:27.210
Why should I worry about her?

01:35:28.060 --> 01:35:29.960
All I gotta do is just say goodbye and that's the end of it.

01:35:30.000 --> 01:35:32.810
You don't worry me none.

01:35:33.070 --> 01:35:34.630
No, she don't worry you, too.

01:35:35.140 --> 01:35:37.120
All you gotta do is say goodbye and that's it.

01:35:43.540 --> 01:35:45.120
You certainly are one hungry man.

01:35:45.710 --> 01:35:47.730
Shucks, I got nobody to say goodbye to.

01:35:49.620 --> 01:35:51.380
Any particular way you gonna tell her?

01:35:52.080 --> 01:35:52.720
I'll tell her.

01:35:53.760 --> 01:35:55.590
Sure, but what do you say?

01:35:56.460 --> 01:35:59.970
That's my department. I'll see you at the bus station.

01:36:00.000 --> 01:36:07.540
I checked your bags from the bar, senor.

01:36:08.020 --> 01:36:10.180
Oh, thanks.

01:36:10.620 --> 01:36:11.600
Oh, gracias, senor, gracias.

01:36:12.580 --> 01:36:14.980
I hope you don't mind if I kind of hang around

01:36:14.980 --> 01:36:16.720
and see how you handle the situation.

01:36:17.430 --> 01:36:19.350
Never been very smart with the women myself.

01:36:20.040 --> 01:36:21.600
Maybe you can learn me a thing or two.

01:36:26.500 --> 01:36:27.680
You got to say goodbye?

01:36:28.620 --> 01:36:28.880
Yeah.

01:36:30.000 --> 01:36:32.620
Just say, so long, kid, and that's the end of it.

01:36:32.960 --> 01:36:34.340
Maybe she won't even be here.

01:36:34.520 --> 01:36:35.780
Then you won't have to say nothing.

01:36:36.300 --> 01:36:37.780
That'll make you a happy jack.

01:36:38.430 --> 01:36:39.470
You think maybe she won't, huh?

01:36:40.520 --> 01:36:42.440
Nah, you don't know dames.

01:36:42.780 --> 01:36:43.600
You don't know what they're like.

01:36:43.700 --> 01:36:44.780
They like to get their hooks in you.

01:36:45.180 --> 01:36:46.420
You know what kind of a fuss they make.

01:36:47.210 --> 01:36:47.950
I'll fix it.

01:36:49.260 --> 01:36:50.960
It looks like this is your lucky day.

01:36:51.460 --> 01:36:52.520
I don't see her around.

01:36:53.590 --> 01:36:56.140
Oye, Mr. Gaggin, my friend.

01:36:57.120 --> 01:36:57.840
Buenos dias.

01:36:58.460 --> 01:36:58.820
Audi.

01:37:01.170 --> 01:37:04.050
Hiya, Pancho. I just came over to say so long.

01:37:05.200 --> 01:37:07.600
So long? My sad word.

01:37:08.190 --> 01:37:10.450
But you make me happy if he's not too long.

01:37:11.210 --> 01:37:13.920
Yeah. Uh, about that money...

01:37:13.920 --> 01:37:17.870
Oh, forget it. My horses give me all the bucks I want.

01:37:18.150 --> 01:37:21.570
We all same kind of people. We all born for be broke.

01:37:22.630 --> 01:37:26.390
I don't let you go home in the bus. I take you pony express.

01:37:27.590 --> 01:37:29.550
But you see, aunties, they all busy.

01:37:32.270 --> 01:37:35.060
A moment, a moment, patience, boys.

01:37:36.680 --> 01:37:37.220
Let's go.

01:37:37.780 --> 01:37:39.980
Hey, Pancho, you do me a favor, will you?

01:37:40.140 --> 01:37:42.440
Oh, sure, senor, sure, anything, anything.

01:37:42.780 --> 01:37:45.000
If Pila shows up, will you tell her...

01:37:45.000 --> 01:37:45.180
Pila, Pila.

01:37:48.030 --> 01:37:49.250
Tell her yourself, senor.

01:37:49.980 --> 01:37:51.810
Hey, andale, andale.

01:38:04.220 --> 01:38:07.220
Hello. Remember me?

01:38:07.500 --> 01:38:11.090
Did you have a good time at the fiesta?

01:38:14.580 --> 01:38:17.920
I just stopped over to thank Pancho.

01:38:19.430 --> 01:38:20.430
It's a fellow, Pancho.

01:38:21.820 --> 01:38:25.320
Also, I wanted to thank... What's the name?

01:38:31.660 --> 01:38:35.800
Remember me, dear grandmother, she'd be glad to see you.

01:38:36.730 --> 01:38:38.030
A lot of people be glad to see you.

01:38:43.860 --> 01:38:49.850
I, uh, what I'm trying to say, what I mean.

01:38:51.830 --> 01:38:52.590
Bye, senor.

01:38:57.100 --> 01:38:58.340
Say goodbye to the lady.

01:39:31.720 --> 01:39:33.680
Fillita, tell us what happened to you and the American.

01:39:34.080 --> 01:39:35.770
Yes, yes, tell me. I'm dying to know.

01:39:36.170 --> 01:39:40.750
He asked me, which way to the La Fonda Hotel.

01:39:41.310 --> 01:39:46.940
I told him, I will show you the hotel.

01:39:47.420 --> 01:39:52.160
The next day he gave me the money and I went to pay in another way.

01:39:52.280 --> 01:39:54.580
To see if he liked it more.

01:39:54.780 --> 01:39:56.080
But they were bad.

01:39:57.180 --> 01:39:58.920
Also the man who came to the canteen.

01:40:00.120 --> 01:40:03.080
but I hit her in the head with a bottle.

01:40:03.440 --> 01:40:04.570
Like this!
